  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>membrane</keyword>
  <short_description>Eigenfunctions of the L-shaped membrane.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>L = membrane</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>L = membrane(k)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>L = membrane(k, n)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>membrane(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>k</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a positive integer: the eigenfunction index (default 1).</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>n</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a positive integer: the grid parameter; the result is (2*n+1)-by-(2*n+1) (default 15).</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>L</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a (2*n+1)-by-(2*n+1) matrix: the k-th eigenfunction sampled on the grid.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>
      <b>membrane</b> returns the <b>k</b>-th eigenfunction of the L-shaped
      membrane, sampled on a square <b>(2*n+1)</b>-by-<b>(2*n+1)</b> grid. The
      domain is the square with one quadrant removed; the value is zero on the
      boundary and outside that domain.</p>
    <p>The first eigenfunction (<b>k = 1</b>) is the fundamental mode, a single
      positive bump; higher indices add nodal lines and therefore negative
      values. The result is normalised so its largest magnitude is 1 with a
      positive peak.</p>
    <p>Called with no output argument, <b>membrane</b> draws the surface.</p>
    <p>The eigenfunction is obtained from a finite-difference discretisation of
      the domain solved with a shift-invert eigensolve
      (<b>eigs</b>) for the smallest eigenvalues.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function>eigs</used_function>
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[L = membrane(1, 10);
size(L)
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[L = membrane(1, 15);
[min(L(:)), max(L(:))]
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>draw the surface</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data
        runnable="gui"
      ><![CDATA[f = figure();
surf(membrane(1, 50), 'EdgeColor', 'none');
axis('off');
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
